✅ QUESTION 1: MAXIMUM SUM CIRCULAR SUBARRAY
🔹 Problem Statement

Given a circular integer array nums, return the maximum possible sum of a non-empty subarray of nums.

A circular array means the end of the array connects to the beginning.

📌 Example
Input: nums = [5, -3, 5]
Output: 10
Explanation: The subarray [5, 5] is formed by wrapping around.


Another example:

Input: nums = [-3, -2, -3]
Output: -2
Explanation: Only one element can be chosen.

🔹 Key Idea / Intuition

There are two possible cases:

Case 1️⃣: Subarray does NOT wrap

→ This is just Kadane’s Algorithm (maximum subarray sum).

Case 2️⃣: Subarray WRAPS around

→ Total sum of array − minimum subarray sum

Why?
If you remove the minimum subarray, the remaining elements (from end + start) form the maximum circular subarray.

⚠️ Edge Case

If all numbers are negative, wrapping does not help.
So return the maximum element (Kadane result).

🔹 Algorithm

Use Kadane’s algorithm to find:

maxSubarraySum

minSubarraySum

Compute totalSum of array

Circular max sum = totalSum - minSubarraySum

Final answer:

if (maxSubarraySum < 0)
    return maxSubarraySum;
else
    return max(maxSubarraySum, totalSum - minSubarraySum);

🔹 Time & Space Complexity

Time: O(N)

Space: O(1)

🔹 Java Code (Clean & Interview-Ready)
class Solution {
    public int maxSubarraySumCircular(int[] nums) {
        int totalSum = 0;

        int maxSum = nums[0];
        int currMax = 0;

        int minSum = nums[0];
        int currMin = 0;

        for (int num : nums) {
            // Kadane for max subarray
            currMax = Math.max(num, currMax + num);
            maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, currMax);

            // Kadane for min subarray
            currMin = Math.min(num, currMin + num);
            minSum = Math.min(minSum, currMin);

            totalSum += num;
        }

        // If all numbers are negative
        if (maxSum < 0) {
            return maxSum;
        }

        return Math.max(maxSum, totalSum - minSum);
    }
}

